         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Introduction\n\nIn the previous class we learned how to measure the length of an object in a single direction, along the horizontal ruler. But objects, people and plants are not lines. They also have height, width and other characteristics, so we need to learn how to measure in other directions as well.\n\nIn this class we are going to learn how to measure in two directions: horizontal and vertical.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "deead311-df32-4b5e-9995-175f732b879f",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "deead311-df32-4b5e-9995-175f732b879f",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "happy",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "add8bb98-aa8c-4373-ad82-3c22b9bf945e",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=add8bb98-aa8c-4373-ad82-3c22b9bf945e",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Step by Step\n\nThe good news is that you already know the method. Measuring with a vertical ruler follows the same steps:\n\n- Place the ruler along the edge of the object, so that one end of the object lines up with the 0 mark.\n- Keep the object straight, without tilting it, and look at the mark where the other end stops.\n- The number at that mark is the measure of the object: it tells the height of the object in the vertical direction.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "35b25e72-c6ff-471e-948a-f39d31513af4",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "35b25e72-c6ff-471e-948a-f39d31513af4",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "inlove",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "add8bb98-aa8c-4373-ad82-3c22b9bf945e",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=add8bb98-aa8c-4373-ad82-3c22b9bf945e",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Example\n\nLook at the square beside the vertical ruler below. It starts at 0 and ends at the mark 5, so its height is 5.\n\nThe ruler goes from 0 to 10, so it can measure any height up to 10. The square occupies the first 5 marks, from the bottom to the top.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "49878049-6282-4917-95d3-e3b1a9ffc550",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "49878049-6282-4917-95d3-e3b1a9ffc550",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "thinking",
         "source_menu": [],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Let Us Think!\n\nOne direction tells us only part of the story.\n\nCan we measure in both directions, horizontal and vertical, to compare two objects better?",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "6a69817b-3b2e-40d3-9fb4-a02d28e666aa",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": "yes",
         "score": 2,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "6a69817b-3b2e-40d3-9fb4-a02d28e666aa",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "shocking",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "add8bb98-aa8c-4373-ad82-3c22b9bf945e",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=add8bb98-aa8c-4373-ad82-3c22b9bf945e",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Comparing\n\nTwo rectangles are fully equal only when they have the same width and the same height.\n\nThe rulers at the top and at the bottom show the width, and the ruler beside each rectangle shows the height.\n\nOn the next screen you will test this idea with the app.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "c6038674-67ac-41ce-b1e2-938746e02bd3",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "c6038674-67ac-41ce-b1e2-938746e02bd3",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "happy",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "add8bb98-aa8c-4373-ad82-3c22b9bf945e",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=add8bb98-aa8c-4373-ad82-3c22b9bf945e",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Practice\n\nPress the plus and minus buttons to change the width and the height of each rectangle, and read the sentence that appears below.\n\nTry to make rectangle 1 equal to rectangle 2.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
